; bfsodium BYTEPAD136 : NIST SP 800_185's bytepad of two encoded strings
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; keccak/leftenc is PASTED twice and chacha20/add32 is
; PASTED twice  once inside each of the two doubling loops;
;
; INTERFACE entry=259 exit=264 footprint=0:451
; IO  in:  nlen{2} LE  slen{2} LE  nbuf{128}  sbuf{128}   (260 bytes)
;     out: one block of a hundred and thirty six bytes
;
; This is  in the standard's own notation
;   bytepad( encode_string(N) then encode_string(S)  136 )
; which is what cSHAKE256 and KMAC256 put on the tape before the message;
; the hundred and thirty six is SHAKE256's rate and it is in the file name
; because A RATE CANNOT BE A PARAMETER HERE: it sets the size of the block
; buffer  which is a tape map and not a number; the 168 twin is a separate
; file for the reason sponge136 and sponge168 are separate files;
;
; NLEN PLUS SLEN MUST BE AT MOST A HUNDRED AND TWENTY EIGHT; the block holds
; two for left_encode of the rate  then each string behind its own length
; encoding of two or three bytes  so the worst case is a hundred and thirty
; six less two less three less three; The routine DOES NOT CHECK IT and a
; caller that breaks it pushes bytes off the end of the block;
;
; THE BLOCK IS BUILT RIGHT TO LEFT  BY PREPENDING  and that is the whole idea
; of this file; The standard's layout puts each piece at an offset that the
; lengths of the pieces before it decide  which is an index  which this
; library does not have; So the pieces go in BACKWARDS  last one first  and
; each one is put in by sliding the whole block right by its length and then
; ADDING it at cell nought; CELL NOUGHT IS ALWAYS CELL NOUGHT  so no position
; is ever computed;
;
; Two things fall out of that and both are wanted; the tail of the block is
; never written  so it stays at nought  which IS bytepad's padding; and the
; pieces beyond a string's own length are nought  so adding a whole buffer
; over the top of the slid block cannot disturb what is already there;
;
; EIGHT TIMES A LENGTH IS THREE DOUBLINGS; encode_string takes the length in
; BITS  and a doubling is chacha20/add32 with the accumulator as its own
; addend  so the multiply is a loop of three around a proved adder rather
; than a fourth hand rolled shift;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  nlen{2}  u16 LE  N's length in BYTES; its high byte is nought
;   @0x002:0x003  slen{2}  u16 LE  S's length in bytes
;   @0x004:0x083  nbuf{128} u8     N  as given; SPENT into the block
;   @0x084:0x103  sbuf{128} u8     S  as given; SPENT into the block
;   @0x108:0x18f  block{136} u8    the answer  built from its right hand end
;   @0x194        k       u8   how many places the next prepend slides by
;   @0x195        t       u8   the cell a byte is copied through
;   @0x196        b       u8   and handed back through
;   @0x197        dbl     u8   the three doublings still to do
;   @0x198:0x19b  tmp{4}  u8   hands the accumulator back to itself
;   @0x19c:0x1ad  keccak/leftenc's frame  pasted at @0x19c; footprint 0:17
;                 its x{4} is at @0x19c  its count at @0x1a8  its bytes
;                 at @0x1a9
;   @0x1b0:0x1c3  chacha20/add32's frame  pasted at @0x1b0; footprint 0:19
;                 its a{4} is the accumulator and its b{4} the addend

; read the two lengths and the two buffers
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
